  "result": "`%TypedArray%.prototype.sort` is implemented in `prototype_sort.rs` (the only file changed), with each spec step as a comment above its code. `./t262 built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/sort/` gives 60 of 70 runs passing and clippy is clean. The 10 failures are all \"not implemented\" errors from other stubs: the BigInt global (`big_int/constructor.rs`) for the BigInt tests, and `Array.prototype.reverse` for `stability.js`. The ticket's \"every run passes\" condition is therefore not met until those land.\n\nThe implementation reuses the existing `sort_indexed_properties` from the Array sort module, and I wrote `CompareTypedArrayElements` inside my file since nothing shared existed. The one non-spec branch is a mismatched Number/BigInt pair in the comparison, which throws a TypeError; the spec's assert says this cannot happen.\n\nBLOCKED: the BigInt constructor (`crates/kahvi-builtins/src/big_int/constructor.rs`) and `Array.prototype.reverse` (`crates/kahvi-builtins/src/array/prototype_reverse.rs`) are still stubs, so 10 of the sort tests cannot pass yet.",
